From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iio: accel: st_accel: allow LIS2HH12 power-on startup

Wait 30 ms after enabling the LIS2HH12/K2HH supplies before accessing
WHO_AM_I, matching the Samsung K2HH power-on sequence. Immediate access
returns -ENXIO on SM-T531 when the supplies were off. The sensor binds
and exports acceleration through IIO once the startup delay is observed.
Other accelerometer variants retain their existing timing.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/iio/accel/st_accel_i2c.c b/drivers/iio/accel/st_accel_i2c.c
--- a/drivers/iio/accel/st_accel_i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/accel/st_accel_i2c.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/pm.h>
 #include <linux/i2c.h>
 #include <linux/iio/iio.h>
@@ -199,6 +200,10 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* Allow LIS2HH12/K2HH power-on startup before reading WHO_AM_I. */
+	if (!strcmp(client->name, "lis2hh12"))
+		msleep(30);
+
 	return st_accel_common_probe(indio_dev);
 }
 
